have. We're now going to move on to talk about in a little more detail, how can we have measures

00:38:56.052 --> 00:39:01.732
that tell us what a document is about? So we're going to talk about a couple of

00:39:02.933 --> 00:39:08.852
statistics that you can measure about a document and how to combine them. So term frequency is just

00:39:08.852 --> 00:39:15.093
like what I was telling you before. Counting. Counting. Usually dividing by the length of the

00:39:15.093 --> 00:39:23.813
document. So some if Don Quixote says Quixote, Quixote, Quixote, over and over and over again,

00:39:23.813 --> 00:39:32.533
that has a high term frequency. Inverse document frequency is this. So this is not something that

00:39:32.533 --> 00:39:39.572
has a theory behind it. It's just a heuristic. But it's a natural log of the number of documents

00:39:39.572 --> 00:39:44.693
you have in a collection divided by the number of documents containing that term. So let's say we

00:39:44.693 --> 00:39:54.292
have many books. Let's say we have 100 books. And then we divide by the number of documents that

00:39:54.292 --> 00:40:03.892
contain that term. So I have 100 books. And only one of them has Quixote in them. So that means we

00:40:03.892 --> 00:40:09.172
have a big number divided by a small number. And we get the natural log. So that's a big number.

00:40:10.052 --> 00:40:17.093
Let's say we have 100 books. And let's say they all have ‑‑ they're English books. They all

00:40:17.093 --> 00:40:22.052
have the word the in them. So then that's one. And the natural log of one is zero. So that

00:40:22.052 --> 00:40:26.452
is a small number. That weights it down. So if you multiply these two numbers together,

00:40:27.653 --> 00:40:33.812
what you get is called TFIDF. So it's the term frequency multiplied by the inverse document

00:40:33.812 --> 00:40:43.332
frequency. So it's like a weighting. Okay, which words are common but are common in one document

00:40:43.332 --> 00:40:50.213
compared to the other ones? It's about comparing documents within a collection. So TFIDF is a way

00:40:50.452 --> 00:40:56.932
to weight counts. A way to weight counts. And what it gives us is a measure of what a document is

00:40:56.932 --> 00:41:03.973
about or how we can find out which words are important in one document compared to other

